{:event/id #uuid "1683159c-b777-4793-999f-d8157a066692", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-08-30T03:32:45.832Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/0d23a6d476fc/worktrees/rheos-roundtrip"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/0d23a6d476fc/worktrees/rheos-roundtrip", :lesson "A regression test can be syntactically green yet absent: run clj-kondo before trusting counts because its inline-def warning exposed a nested deftest here. When an existing tracked fixture contains a NUL byte and Git treats it as binary, keep new cases in a separate text test namespace so review evidence stays inspectable. Managed pnpm may stop at ignored-build policy before any build; preserve that policy, record the blocked broad gate, and use package-local pinned binaries for scoped evidence rather than mutating supply-chain configuration."}}
{:event/id #uuid "fd1ebfd0-c44a-4103-a0a8-7af131f5ed61", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-08-30T07:01:38.998Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/8d4eacbf051e/eta-rheos-planning"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/8d4eacbf051e/eta-rheos-planning", :lesson "Hosted evidence can lawfully clear a local environment blocker only when it binds the exact published tree and covers the blocked broad gates; record that proof before walking the canonical FSM, and keep review distinct from completion until the metadata successor itself is published and independently reviewed."}}
{:event/id #uuid "59daa6d8-ba38-4c37-9608-ad18353f366f", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-08-30T07:31:52.004Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/8d4eacbf051e/eta-rheos-planning"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/8d4eacbf051e/eta-rheos-planning", :lesson "When structured IDs are serialized by a deliberately small frontmatter writer, nonblank validation is insufficient: bind accepted IDs to the same line-safe grammar as their canonical identity and add no-write injection tests at the effect boundary. Review findings against append-only and serializer authority before applying plausible byte edits."}}
{:event/id #uuid "10aa03dc-6b0d-44f0-a13a-1bf347f3cb77", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-08-30T08:01:19.574Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/8d4eacbf051e/eta-frontmatter-serialization-card"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/8d4eacbf051e/eta-frontmatter-serialization-card", :lesson "A card-only security owner must be generated with landed command authority: an otherwise canonical write from a frozen successor can leak that successor's unmerged metadata into the owner record. Guard the artifact revision, inspect raw card and ledger bytes, and regenerate before publication when the authority differs."}}
{:event/id #uuid "df88d437-47d4-4fdb-8ab3-6f20ab68ed76", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-09T19:38:22.715Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/aa97e77e8c32/eta-mu-sol-bootstrap"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/aa97e77e8c32/eta-mu-sol-bootstrap", :lesson "A pre-merge test workflow must be bootstrapped independently on trusted default-branch machinery; merging its target to make the test runnable cannot establish pre-merge evidence. Keep the actual exact-SHA human promotion distinct from broad task authorization."}}
{:event/id #uuid "cdaf484b-12ef-4897-bcfc-e8b53d95909c", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-09T19:59:43.255Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/aa97e77e8c32/eta-mu-sol-bootstrap"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/aa97e77e8c32/eta-mu-sol-bootstrap", :lesson "Friction3/5: API mocks must model SDK-normalized list responses rather than raw REST envelopes; bind deployment policy checks to actual bypass settings and execute extracted warning gates against zero-exit diagnostic fixtures. Independent review and red-before-green regressions exposed gaps that syntax-only contracts missed."}}
{:event/id #uuid "276f2663-9855-4e52-bb7d-31bb75f685c5", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-11T23:48:19.942Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/foresight/eta-mu-clio-dev"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/foresight/eta-mu-clio-dev", :lesson "Clio is the canonical ledger, and provider adapters must retain wire payload contracts while delegating schema hashes, identity, admission and causal replay to that kernel. JVM and Node interoperability tests expose durable lock guarantees that in-memory fixtures cannot cover. A frozen offline lock validation can reuse existing pinned native dependencies without re-resolving unrelated package metadata."}}
{:event/id #uuid "9c04c5df-784f-4dae-9d2a-107951d5418a", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-12T00:13:23.090Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/foresight/eta-mu-clio-dev"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/foresight/eta-mu-clio-dev", :lesson "Current guidance and dated survey history need separate labels during a provider retirement. Reconciled Clio ownership, service payload boundaries and Rheos raw-envelope compatibility against actual manifests while retaining the August survey. Reading both package.json and bb.edn exposed divergent build targets; documentation now names the difference instead of claiming the commands are interchangeable."}}
{:event/id #uuid "14db9064-d331-4331-bb0c-1dc97db030e5", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-12T00:22:10.325Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/foresight/eta-mu-clio-dev"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/foresight/eta-mu-clio-dev", :lesson "A ClojureScript with-redefs replacement must preserve the compiled callable shape of the real boundary, not only accept the same apparent arguments. Receipt River production git/exec-at has two arities, so callers use its arity-2 dispatch property; a single-arity delayed fixture lacked it. Reproduced before changing the fixture, retained every concurrency assertion and timer, and verified package tests, production release and lint."}}
{:event/id #uuid "c5a40627-bb89-4426-bc94-ae17ea19ba7c", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-12T07:25:47.418Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-clio-foundation"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-clio-foundation", :lesson "Sol concurrent wire retry repair: p-efficiency0.9, p-friction0.2, p-skill-candidate0.3. A sequential retry test missed an unlocked planning race. Two independent handles with deterministic preemption at the real append boundary reproduced the canonical UUID/time conflict, then verified first-fact reuse and strict competing-payload refusal. Existing falsify-every-new-test and verify-the-binary lessons apply; no new spore."}}
{:event/id #uuid "ae4265a1-cbb9-468a-b02f-e1a5d5f7868f", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-12T07:58:14.835Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-clio-foundation"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-clio-foundation", :lesson "Clio PR334 Node durability review: instrument the mutable CommonJS fs default and refresh built-in ESM exports before trusting fsync observations; immutable namespace patches silently observed nothing. A real baseline admitted events without schema temp/directory sync. Now schema content, atomic publication, empty ledger and ancestry are forced before acknowledgement; a partial directory failure retries existing ancestry. Friction 0.4: ptrace is unavailable in this sandbox, so evidence proves actual native-call sequencing and refusal, not physical power-loss durability. Full Clio BB25/75 JVM61/164 NBB62/151 Shadow62/151 passed with zero failures/errors, lint and compile zero warnings. No spore incubated."}}
{:event/id #uuid "85ba45fa-f575-4a04-8f73-821d2d0f5c0a", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-12T08:21:51.313Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-clio-foundation"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-clio-foundation", :lesson "Warning-gate review: p-efficiency 0.85, p-friction 0.25, p-skill-candidate 0.3; no new spore. Executing the actual generated Bash and local CLI with successful processes that emit lowercase, comma-ended, bracketed Maven and positive-count warnings reproduced missed failures. Keep zero-warning and original-exit controls beside each rejection. Evidence: package-warning-gates-red/green, generated-warning-gates-red/green, warning-gates-full-cli-tests."}}
{:event/id #uuid "6981ed92-07b1-4ca3-bf03-cbc54b543d84", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-12T08:25:08.131Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-identity-work"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-identity-work", :lesson "Axxium review checkpoint a7b19825: efficiency 0.8, friction 0.35. Existing worktree recovery retained source commits but omitted later lawful card transitions; verify canonical card projection instead of trusting an earlier success message. A nonblocking cleanup finally can mask an already-committed signup, so preserve results and retain expiring leases on deferred cleanup. Account fallback safety depends on configured methods, not just stored bindings. Integrated source gates pass 66 tests/632 assertions and real TCP proof; strict legacy boundary remains 56 violations and live external consent is distinct. Existing recovery and exact-head spores cover these lessons; no new spore incubated."}}
{:event/id #uuid "2d681fb4-6f19-462b-b9f4-609c23a5fddc", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-12T09:29:02.279Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-foundation-openfix"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-foundation-openfix", :lesson "PR334 shared EDN opener: P-efficiency 0.8, P-friction 0.5, skill-candidate 0.4. Exact published source recovery worked after sandbox loss; canonical CLIs required rebuild. Sol first-open recovery did not cover the separate shared-services opener. A real two-process barrier reproduced native EEXIST, then proved winner replay and both durable writes. Full guarded protocols 71/217, strict TS, ESM111 files0warnings and kondo0/0 green. Review transition refused before broad build because unactivated shell chose runtime pnpm; card remains in_progress, with no bypass or false broad-gate claim. No new spore."}}
{:event/id #uuid "ce97e6a6-470a-4d5d-9cef-07d43972e7fc", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-12T09:57:30.194Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-foundation-openfix"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-foundation-openfix", :lesson "PR334 review friction 3/5: a per-stream CAS cannot enforce a cross-stream Sol wire identity. Serialize the wire-ID decision and canonical append using a separate kernel-locked inode, then replay-check old histories for duplicate wire IDs. Test the actual two-process boundary and rejected inode-fsync acknowledgement, not only single-writer success. Linux retains durable EDN; unsupported Node hosts must select explicit volatile behavior instead of failing an ordinary turn."}}
{:event/id #uuid "23d0cdb5-148c-43f3-9105-ba636a293092", :event/type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-09-12T10:02:00.872Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu session reflect"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-identity-work"}, :event/payload {:repo "/workspace/scratch/3655842e43cf/eta-identity-work", :lesson "One-use provider exchange and local admission have different retry boundaries: keep the verified result across native lock contention, but revalidate current finite challenge and linking authority before every commit. Actual SDK/module and HTTP-header tests caught bcrypt import and cookie unit defects that adapter mocks missed. Guarded Axxium 83/744, build 119 files zero warnings, lint and unchanged strict boundary zero; live provider consent remains separately unverified. Existing review-thread and exact-head lessons cover this slice; no new spore."}}
#:event{:id #uuid "f9629cde-aa9b-43ef-838e-3f2ecea595e6", :type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :recorded-at "2026-09-12T11:42:58.073Z", :schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "recovery.write-review-receipts"}, :subject #:repository{:path "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-identity"}, :payload {:repo "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-identity", :lesson "Recovery friction0.6, efficiency0.8, skill-candidate0.4; no new spore. Distinguish visible bytes from durable acknowledgment at every provider no-op. Real SDK callback fixtures must include the issuer DPoP key; stubbing only outer callback misses session-store failures. Preserve every historical ledger byte when merging independent append histories; fail a combined shell step before staging on script failure. Pinned source recovery plus fresh guards establishes new evidence, never transfers lost-tree results."}}
#:event{:id #uuid "338b5fb3-8108-4dbe-b640-f8ff5b316bd4", :type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :recorded-at "2026-09-12T12:00:20.954Z", :schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "recovery.write-review-receipts"}, :subject #:repository{:path "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-foundation"}, :payload {:repo "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-foundation", :lesson "Creation, append, and projection acknowledgments are distinct failure paths. Test each through real native descriptors and the public consuming provider; visibility and matching state do not prove a completed durability fence. Preserve uncertain files, validate their facts, and force inode plus parent on recovery."}}
#:event{:id #uuid "9f6af1ad-e9bc-4909-b2ab-162287a89fa2", :type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :recorded-at "2026-09-12T12:09:20.788Z", :schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "recovery.write-review-receipts"}, :subject #:repository{:path "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-identity-successor"}, :payload {:repo "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-identity-successor", :lesson "A reference SDK storage test is insufficient unless the application orchestration is also exercised with distinct SDK and application state. Keep native SDK behavior real and only control the remote issuer. Pin independent consumers to immutable source copies; notifying one compiler owner does not release another consumer freeze."}}
#:event{:id #uuid "2593331a-cd4a-4827-bb35-01b207f68c9b", :type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :recorded-at "2026-09-12T12:32:15.750Z", :schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "recovery.write-review-receipts"}, :subject #:repository{:path "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-foundation-snapshot"}, :payload {:repo "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-foundation-snapshot", :lesson "Read-side projection capture must use the writer inode lock even when validation and folding remain pure. Freeze source paths per consumer and publish a distinct immutable successor before asking dependent projects to rerun; never transfer gate totals from an older kernel."}}
#:event{:id #uuid "633ea889-6cd5-4d50-bd7b-5db734012c69", :type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :recorded-at "2026-09-12T12:43:22.465Z", :schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "recovery.write-review-receipts"}, :subject #:repository{:path "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-identity-initialization"}, :payload {:repo "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-identity-initialization", :lesson "Durable private state must be fenced independently of public facts. Reserve expensive proof work before invoking crypto, retain failed or uncertain reservations across restart, and decide administrator grants from current transaction facts. Read review assertions critically; a no-findings review does not erase another reviewer concrete reproducer or replace exact source verification."}}
#:event{:id #uuid "ecb0e24c-7ad8-4f7c-9a3d-6d28f28995fe", :type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :recorded-at "2026-09-12T12:48:48.580Z", :schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "recovery.write-review-receipts"}, :subject #:repository{:path "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-foundation-ci"}, :payload {:repo "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-foundation-ci", :lesson "Path-triggered CI coverage is not established by a workflow name or a green unrelated package. Test the actual authoritative workflow registry and generated shell, require real package assertion output, preserve nonzero and warning failure, then verify the published hosted run."}}
#:event{:id #uuid "1293d3d7-5aa5-43a1-b695-704511752da2", :type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :recorded-at "2026-09-12T13:31:12.596Z", :schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "recovery.write-review-receipts"}, :subject #:repository{:path "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-foundation-single"}, :payload {:repo "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-foundation-single", :lesson "A public reader and a printable identifier are not automatically safe: use the owning native lock for every ledger snapshot and require exact kind/namespace/name EDN roundtrip before admitting identifier bytes. Treat successful exit with compiler warnings as a failed gate."}}
#:event{:id #uuid "3fc45f50-d241-4f78-bd1d-a1ea4b6a0be9", :type :session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :recorded-at "2026-09-12T13:52:14.203Z", :schema {:id :eta-mu.session-mycology/reflection-recorded, :version 1}, :producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/session-mycology", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "recovery.write-review-receipts"}, :subject #:repository{:path "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-identity-grants"}, :payload {:repo "/workspace/foresight-active/worktrees/eta-identity-grants", :lesson "An identity append can become visible before durability while its response contains a one-use token: retain one prepared event/result and re-fence only that exact event. Provider creation is not the end of initialization; concurrent ATProto route registration must choose the accepted key under current admission."}}
